WEBVTT

00:10:00.162 --> 00:10:03.412
So just just as a little bit
of back story, every year,

00:10:03.412 --> 00:10:05.746
I have students at the undergrad
level apply to my class.

00:10:06.121 --> 00:10:10.704
And one of the questions is, what's your
favorite TED talk? Yours is every year.

00:10:10.746 --> 00:10:15.204
One of the topics I think one of the
things that jumped out at me after

00:10:15.204 --> 00:10:19.037
the first few years was it was mostly
women who were naming you

00:10:19.037 --> 00:10:22.079
as their favorite talk. And and I'm
wondering, I'm sure some of this,

00:10:22.079 --> 00:10:24.579
of course, is, you know, men tend
to choose male role models.

00:10:24.579 --> 00:10:25.871
Women tend to choose female.

00:10:26.329 --> 00:10:31.162
But it also seems like vulnerability
is easier for women to process